**Recommendation: Redis Streams.** The decisive axes are the constraints, not raw capability: 6-person team with zero Kafka experience and no infra engineer, ≤2-week window, modest budget, Redis already in production. Kafka wins on throughput, retention/replay, and rebalancing, but its ceiling is irrelevant at the projected 10x peak (~10–25k msgs/s), and its headline differentiator — exactly-once semantics — cannot extend to external webhook/email providers anyway; the real guarantee is consumer-side dedupe, which both options require. The document also specifies the target architecture (XADD producer, XREADGROUP workers with backoff, XCLAIM, DLQ, Postgres dedupe for billing) and a Kafka-swappable interface so the choice stays low-regret.

Structure matches the spec exactly: Title → Status → Context → Decision (with rationale) → Consequences (positive/negative/follow-ups) → Alternatives Considered (Kafka rejected; SQS/SNS and Postgres-as-queue scoped out briefly).

